Subject: build with bionic: in_addr_t, IN6_IS_ADDR_UNSPECIFIED, index/rindex, strdupa

Why:
- iproute2 compiles with -Iinclude/uapi, so its own uapi <linux/in6.h> shadows the bionic sysroot copy,
  which is where bionic gets in_addr_t; typedef it there.
- bionic's IN6_IS_ADDR_UNSPECIFIED() takes a struct in6_addr *, lib/utils.c passes __u32[]; use a
  local array version.
- bionic has no BSD index()/rindex() declarations (not in <strings.h>); use strchr()/strrchr().
- bionic has no strdupa(); define it with alloca() where it is used.
- bionic has no getpass() (ip sr hmac set prompts for a key); add a small termios-based one in
  ip/ipseg6.c (written for this module; Termux gets getpass from libandroid-support instead).
- bionic's libc.a defines an undeclared bpf() syscall stub, so lib/bpf_glue.c's bpf() is a duplicate
  symbol in a static link; rename it via include/bpf_util.h (written for this module).
Source: adapted from termux-packages packages/iproute2/{in_addr_t,IN6_IS_ADDR_UNSPECIFIED,rindex,
strdupa}.patch at commit e187f140fbaf3539de31549c1fed8211a2ac94d2 (2026-11-01), rebased to 7.3.0.
Termux's sethostent.patch (API < 28 only) and libandroid-glob (bionic has glob() since API 28) are
not needed at API 29; Makefile.patch only moves paths into the Termux prefix and is not used.

